Task: structured-logging audit + retrofit (Phase 4c, ADR 0010).

Audited every log line Phases 1-3 emit, per the scope boundary agreed
before starting this task: this module's own combinators only know
generic things about a Kafka record (topic/partition/offset at most) -
never eventType/correlationId, which require decoding a service-specific
payload and stay the calling service's job.

Retry/CircuitBreaker (purekafka.resilience): fully generic over F[A], no
Kafka-specific context (not even topic) available at all - nothing to
retrofit.
StreamSupervisor (purekafka.consumer): generic over Stream[F, O], also
has no per-record context available (it restarts a whole stream-build
action, not a single record) - nothing to retrofit.
DeadLetter.guard (purekafka.consumer): the only combinator that actually
has topic/key in scope. Its log line used plain string interpolation
(s"...$dlqTopic...$key") rather than structured context - retrofitted
to logger.error(Map(topic, dlq_topic, key), error)(message), matching
this codebase's existing structured-logging convention.

No generic eventType/correlationId extraction logic was added anywhere -
confirmed out of scope and left that way.

